   "html": "<p>Sineda's cousin, a Pict of Jagent who keeps the old gods. His uncles on his father's side are knights, and he has four younger sisters and a younger brother. At the Midsummer feast he held the attention of a young lady of good family all evening, and asked the Earl's leave to court her, and was told to come back when he was a knight.</p>\n<p>Drust has dreamed of the banner, more clearly than any of the others. He means to hold a straight line in a crooked world, and would rather be a song than a statue. Lord Clefford is having him dressed properly, and taught to read.</p>"
